{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And He has set you apart today — singled you out, that you declared and agreed to be a people to Him, because He performed signs and mighty deeds, so you agreed — to be a people to Him. האמרת in Old French is *feire*."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss פאישדי\"רא is uncertain; it may represent a dialectal or Picard form of *feire* ('to do/make'). The Hebrew lemma is cited in shortened form from וגם הוא האמירך היום."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:32.622318496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}